{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Navi",
  "theme": "navi",
  "_about": "Navi, after a photo of a BMW map view (Nov 14 2026), generated by tools/gen_mblade_navi.py (edit that and regenerate): a wide diagonal speed band on the left (textured blue stripe, violet stripe, a white marker at the speed on the same scale as the Sport theme), the big rounded map window with the white line under it that steps up at the right, and thin bars along the bottom: fuel with its range on the left, the hybrid battery with its electric range on the right (in place of the photo's oil temperature, which moves to the free column on the right). The stock-style shift light and the lettering are at the top. Without a map window the gear and the speed are big in the middle; with one (Waze, Cluster Centre, Cluster Info) the theme is rebuilt as the Sport theme is (backdrop_open and the o_ readouts): the window at x 534..1386, y 120..600, the band steeper and narrower on the left, the gear and speed big on the right above BMW's black box, nothing under the map. Clear of BMW's belt light (x 587..626, y 663..700). Widget reference: shared/hud.js header.",
